   "line": [
    "c6"
   ],
   "spoken": "Then the c6 setup — a pawn to c6 with a specific purpose.",
   "kind": "main"
  },
  {
   "ply": 9,
   "t": 168,
   "fen": "rnbqkb1r/pp3ppp/2p2n2/3pp3/8/PP4PP/2PPPPB1/RNBQK1NR b KQkq - 1 5",
   "line": [
    "Bg2"
   ],
   "spoken": "White fianchettoes, and the bishop on g2 immediately bites on granite: it stares at the d5-pawn, which our pawn chain defends beautifully, so the bishop is nearly useless. The knight will develop via d7 and reroute f8-g6 rather than block it.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": [
    "blunt the fianchetto bishop with the c6/d5 wall"
   ]
  },
